NAME
    df - report file system space usage

SYNOPSIS
    df [OPTION] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Shows the amount of space used and available on each mounted
    file system. VNU's only real file system is the in-memory VFS
    (mounted on /); /dev and /proc are pseudo file systems with
    no accounted space, so they print zeros. FILE operands restrict
    the report to the file systems containing those files.

    Sizes are shown in 1 KiB blocks unless a human-readable option
    is given.

OPTIONS
    -a            include pseudo file systems (all are shown anyway)
    -h            human-readable sizes (powers of 1024)
    -H            human-readable sizes (powers of 1000)
    -k            show sizes in 1 KiB blocks (the default)
    -l            limit to local file systems (all are local)
    -P            POSIX output format (1024-blocks, single spaces)
    -T            also print the file system type
    -t TYPE       only include file systems of type TYPE
    -x TYPE       exclude file systems of type TYPE
    -v            ignored (macOS compatibility)
        --help    display this help and exit
        --version output version information and exit

EXAMPLES
    df
    df -h /proc/version
    df -T -t vfs
